// Terrain types (ADR-0005). Loaded by trpg_content::terrain.
//
// Rules (move_cost, defense, avoid, heal_percent) are game design:
// all come from docs/design/terrain.md and are TUNABLE. Healing tiles are
// deferred there, so heal_percent is 0 everywhere. The building tiles are
// `fort`, `house`, `gate` and `throne` (ticket 0037).
//
// Look (glyphs, fg, bg) follows docs/design/look-and-feel.md (ticket 0011):
// `glyphs` is exactly two characters (a map tile is two cells wide, ADR-0018)
// that the font atlas must contain; `fg` / `bg` are colour names from
// palette.ron, bg being the terrain's own background tint (`<name>_bg`).
//
// move_cost maps every movement type to Some(cost) or None (impassable).
(
    movement_types: ["foot", "mounted", "armored", "flying"],
    terrains: [
        (
            id: "plain", name: "Plain", glyphs: "..", fg: "grass", bg: "grass_bg",
            move_cost: { "foot": Some(1), "mounted": Some(1), "armored": Some(1), "flying": Some(1) },
            defense: 0, avoid: 0, heal_percent: 0,
        ),
        (
            id: "road", name: "Road", glyphs: "··", fg: "road", bg: "road_bg",
            move_cost: { "foot": Some(1), "mounted": Some(1), "armored": Some(1), "flying": Some(1) },
